/E (The most challenging aspect of this project is operating system kernel development using Rust. Since this project involves low-level programming, it requires a deep understanding of computer architecture, memory management, interrupt handling, paging, boot processes, and hardware interaction. Debugging kernel-level code is significantly more difficult than debugging traditional applications because standard debugging tools and operating system services are unavailable during early kernel development.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Another major challenge is integrating artificial intelligence into the operating system while maintaining a secure separation between the kernel and AI services. Designing a reliable communication mechanism, processing system logs, interpreting AI responses, and ensuring that AI recommendations do not compromise system stability require careful architectural decisions. Time management is also a significant challenge, given the compressed 60-day timeline: the project combines learning advanced systems programming concepts with implementing a complete prototype in roughly two-thirds the time of a standard OJT cycle. Memory management \(Week 4\) is)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
